<!--
  The canonical, public, indexable pages, and only those.

  No `priority` and no `changefreq`: Google ignores both, and the pair of them
  going stale is a maintenance cost with nothing at the other end of it.

  The application's own routes are deliberately absent. `/?world=<id>`, the
  planet viewers under /planet_explorer/, /transit/ and /geohub/ are states of
  one application rather than pages, and every one of them either bounces to
  the shell or carries a canonical pointing at the page that describes it.
  What a crawler should land on is the page that explains what the application
  does; those pages are the ones listed here.
-->
